%N A402352 Numbers that are neither squarefree, powerful, nor highly composite.
%C A402352 Apart from {1, 2, 4, 6, 36}, highly composite numbers are neither squarefree nor powerful (in A332785).
%C A402352 Numbers k that are neither squarefree nor squareful such that there exists another number m < k with at least as many divisors as k has.
%C A402352 Proper subset of A402349.
%C A402352 Superset of A387919, in turn a superset of A386294.
%H A402352 Michael De Vlieger, <a href="/A402352/b402352.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A402352 {a(n)} = A332785 \ A002182.
%F A402352 A002182 = Union of {1, 2, 4, 6, 36} and A332785 \ {a(n)}.
%e A402352 Let d = A000005 and let h be the largest highly composite number that does not exceed a(n).
%e A402352 Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..12:
%e A402352    n  a(n)  d(a(n))   d(h)
%e A402352   ------------------------------
%e A402352    1   18      6      d(12) =  6
